<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 1, third movement (Gustav Mahler)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, in a minor key</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Frère Jacques, play (Henri Bernstein and Pierre Veber)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1904</span><span class="sg-chain-h">title only</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Revolution of the Citizens (國民革命歌)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1926</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">What Makes Music Symphonic? (Leonard Bernstein, Young People's Concerts)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Paperback Writer (The Beatles)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1966</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Surf's Up (The Beach Boys)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in (the English version, in words and melody)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Young, Dumb, Stupid (Nmixx)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2023</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Two Tigers (Chinese children's song)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new words</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Capriccio Fra Jacopino sopra L'Aria Di Ruggiero (Girolamo Frescobaldi)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">c. 1615</span><span class="sg-chain-h">similar melody (resemblance only)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Chanson de Lambert</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1650</span><span class="sg-chain-h">similar melody (resemblance only)</span></li></ul></section>
